  "description": "Security and authorization middleware for EIAM. Provides request-signature validation (CypherSecurity), logged-in session validation, and role-based API authorization for ASP.NET Core applications.",
  "id": "EIAM.Package.Security10",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-09-23T14:50:46.043Z",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "A1t5sGidnakcjAEmkRpSnZJtuepR0A8CrJJlWvKKhnRm0N1zIRAMVWbJweMQ3wR6usvJbHE+LFjiZN+HzU+88Q==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 69226,
  "published": "2026-09-23T14:46:04.323Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.10.0 — Cloud mode: setting SecurityApiUrl moves authorization to the EIAM Authorization API over HTTPS, so a Cloud application needs no database credentials. OAuth2 client-credentials authentication to the API with an in-memory cached token; API key, static bearer and caller-token forwarding also supported. Startup validation fails fast on missing or insecure settings. Configurable timeout (default 5s) and optional bounded retries (off by default). Correlation id propagated as X-Correlation-ID. Session ids and signatures are now redacted from logs. Every API failure path denies; the package never fails open. On-premise database behaviour is unchanged. 1.9.4 — Options overload so the database connection is supplied in Program.cs. 1.9.3 — Settings move under a single DAFSetting section. 1.9.2 — EnableSecurityMiddleware and EnableAuthorizationMiddleware switches. 1.9.1 — Targets .NET 10, removes embedded secrets, trims dependencies to 5.",
